<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "backupcheck">
<!ENTITY author "hernandito">
<!ENTITY version "2026.11.26">
<!ENTITY github "hernandito/Backup.Check">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY plugdir "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY cache "/boot/config/plugins/&name;/&version;">
<!ENTITY src "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/&version;">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        launch="/Tools/BackupCheck"
        icon="backupcheck.png"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        support="https://github.com/&github;"
        min="6.12.0">

<CHANGES>
###2026.11.26
- New: a daily summary file. Every morning (09:15) a one-page report of every backup is saved on the flash drive, in config\plugins\backupcheck\summary\Backup Summary - latest.html, with a dated copy for each of the last 14 days.
- The same files are also saved in a "Backup Summary" folder on each backup drive listed in the catalog ("summary": {"copies": [...]}), so a copy survives even if the flash drive fails. A drive that isn't mounted is skipped.
- The summary is a single, self-contained web page (no internet, scripts or other files needed): double-click it on any Windows PC to read it, even when the server is down. Print it to PDF from the browser if you want one.
- The Overview shows where the file is, when it was last saved, and has View and Save now buttons.
- Catalog: the NTFS-Backup rebuild kit is now separate Appdata, Flash and MySQL jobs (daily, weekly, monthly), and Nextcloud to NTFS-Backup runs daily.

###2026.11.20a
- Cleanup Description. Made brief.

###2026.11.20
- Initial release: one dashboard for every backup on the server, organised by the data being protected.
- A card per kind of data: when it was last backed up, every copy (its type and the drive it lands on) grouped daily / weekly / monthly, the last 7 days of each copy, and how far back you can restore.
- Drill in: each copy's full path, a "restore from here" pointer, each job's runs with files new / changed / removed, and the exact list of files a run touched, grouped by folder.
- Jobs and Locations views. Uses the friendly script names set in User Scripts / Script Deck.
- Reads each backup script's own run record, User Scripts schedules, Script Deck history and the Appdata Backup plugin. Read-only: it never changes a backup.

</CHANGES>

<!--
  OFFLINE-SAFE INSTALL
  Unraid re-runs this file at every boot. Each file is kept on the flash drive in a folder named
  after the version (&cache;), so after the first install a boot needs no internet. Downloads are
  pinned to the git tag &version;, and every file is checked against its MD5.
-->
<FILE Name="&cache;/BackupCheck.page"><URL>&src;/BackupCheck.page</URL><MD5>bbf13dfd33e51c19351085ca684c1c1b</MD5></FILE>
